## Context

Found during `/lair` housekeeping (2026-09-04): `make check-fast` reports 2
failures, both pre-existing and unrelated to any work landed today —

```
FAILED tests/test_summarize_0120.py::test_decompose_splits_the_keyword_half_from_the_store - FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'sqlite3'
FAILED tests/test_summarize_0120.py::test_decompose_counts_every_fts_shadow_table_it_declares - FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'sqlite3'
```

The `sqlite3` CLI binary is missing on this machine (padme); the tests shell
out to it rather than using Python's `sqlite3` module. Referenced in
passing across several artifacts this session (`bench/results/0642-work-counters/README.md`,
`bench/results/0643-resume-embedding-perturbation/`) but never tracked.

## Actions

Either install `sqlite3` on this machine, or rewrite the two tests to use
Python's stdlib `sqlite3` module instead of shelling out — the latter is
probably the more portable fix long-term.

## Exit criteria
- `make check-fast` green on this machine without installing anything
  machine-specific, or the missing-binary case is documented as an
  accepted skip with a reason.
